# Handoff docs

When starting a **new chat** about this project, read [`OBJECTIVE.md`](OBJECTIVE.md) and [`PROGRESS.md`](PROGRESS.md) first (and `Saffin profile.txt` if role-fit matters). Do not ask the user to re-explain the whole product.

## When to update
After meaningful work in this repo, update those files in the same session:

1. **OBJECTIVE.md** — if goals, regions, filters, run instructions, or out-of-scope changed.
2. **PROGRESS.md** — mark done items, note new limitations, adjust “Next ideas”, set **Last updated** date.

Keep both concise. Prefer checkboxes and bullets over long narrative.

## Do not
- Duplicate the full chat history into these files.
- Leave PROGRESS stale after shipping a user-visible feature or source fix.
